    "findings": [
      {
        "id": "QR-18.1-01",
        "severity": "HIGH",
        "earliest_owner": "implement",
        "required_correction": true,
        "evidence": "PreparedSourceReadContext.cs:110-113 returns Incomplete for every nonempty canonical RelativeDirectory. The contract's Paths, text and ordering section requires list_prepared_source to return immediate children of the requested directory and enables caller-directed recursive discovery. PreparedSourceListTests.cs only lists the root path \"\".",
        "consequence": "A Worker can discover a directory name at the root but cannot list its children, so nested prepared source is inaccessible through the required list capability. The returned Incomplete outcome also misclassifies an ordinary authorized request.",
        "correction": "Add a public-seam regression test for listing an owned nested directory, then open and enumerate it through the same held-root, handle-relative traversal and return Repository-relative child locations, truthful limits and cursor behavior."
      },
      {
        "id": "QR-18.1-02",
        "severity": "MEDIUM",
        "earliest_owner": "implement",
        "required_correction": true,
        "evidence": "PreparedSourceReadContext.cs:269-414 opens a read handle and checks RandomAccess.GetLength before and after reading, but does not compare ObserveFile identity/last-write metadata. SearchTextAsync does compare ObserveFile at lines 746, 873 and 888. Plan ID-S02/ID-F02 and the contract's safety invariant 4 require detection of observed file identity/metadata drift. PreparedSourceFailureTests.cs has no in-flight same-length read-change case.",
        "consequence": "A same-length rewrite during a read can return Complete and bytes from changing live input even when its last-write metadata changed, making the stated complete observation unreliable.",
        "correction": "Use the existing observed file identity/metadata mechanism around range reads and add a deterministic controlled regression that rewrites the held file to equal length during the operation, with a distinct observed write time; expect ChangedInput without text."
      }
    ],
    "summary": "REVISE. The 115 passing direct controlled tests and clean convergence do not cover nested listing or same-length read drift. The Windows containment, closed Agent schemas, current-authority checks, resource settlement, lookback, and scoped lesson change otherwise match the reviewed design on static inspection. The 63 selected PostgreSQL-backed retained-source regressions were blocked before assertions by the absent VULGATA_STORY131_POSTGRES_ADMIN prerequisite; no real Worker/model/provider integration was claimed. Correct both findings through the existing behavioral TDD owners, refresh invalidated convergence and lookback, then pin a new quality candidate."
  }
